      {"type":"mc","q":"A student is working with this situation: A quadratic that does not factor conveniently is solved using the quadratic formula. Which reasoning is most useful for analyzing it correctly? Consider both the immediate evidence and the broader relationship. Choose the option that remains valid even when the context becomes more complex.","choices":["Polynomial operations combine like terms and use distributive reasoning while preserving coefficients and exponents correctly.","Factoring rewrites an expression as a product of factors and reverses multiplication or distribution.","Exponent properties follow from repeated multiplication and apply consistently to products, quotients, and powers with the same base.","Quadratic equations can be solved by factoring, square roots, completing the square, or the quadratic formula when the method is appropriate."],"answer":"Quadratic equations can be solved by factoring, square roots, completing the square, or the quadratic formula when the method is appropriate.","explain":"Quadratic equations can be solved by factoring, square roots, completing the square, or the quadratic formula when the method is appropriate. The example is connected to quadratic solution, so this option gives the most defensible explanation."},
      {"type":"mc","q":"Simplify 4^4 × 4^2.","choices":["4^6","4^2","4^8","8^6"],"answer":"4^6","explain":"When multiplying powers with the same base, add exponents: 4+2=6."},
      {"type":"mc","q":"Which pair gives the solutions of x² + 9x + -10 = 0?","choices":["x = 1 and x = -9","x = -1 and x = 10","x = 2 and x = -10","x = 1 and x = -10"],"answer":"x = 1 and x = -10","explain":"The quadratic factors as (x - (1))(x - (-10)) = 0."},
      {"type":"mc","q":"Simplify 3^5 × 3^3.","choices":["6^8","3^15","3^8","3^2"],"answer":"3^8","explain":"When multiplying powers with the same base, add exponents: 5+3=8."},
      {"type":"mc","q":"Which pair gives the solutions of x² + -15x + 56 = 0?","choices":["x = -7 and x = -8","x = 7 and x = 9","x = 8 and x = 8","x = 7 and x = 8"],"answer":"x = 7 and x = 8","explain":"The quadratic factors as (x - (7))(x - (8)) = 0."},
      {"type":"mc","q":"Simplify 4^6 × 4^4.","choices":["8^10","4^24","4^2","4^10"],"answer":"4^10","explain":"When multiplying powers with the same base, add exponents: 6+4=10."},
      {"type":"mc","q":"Which pair gives the solutions of x² + -1x + -42 = 0?","choices":["x = -6 and x = 7","x = 6 and x = -7","x = -5 and x = 7","x = -6 and x = 8"],"answer":"x = -6 and x = 7","explain":"The quadratic factors as (x - (-6))(x - (7)) = 0."},
      {"type":"mc","q":"Simplify 2^2 × 2^3.","choices":["4^5","2^6","2^1","2^5"],"answer":"2^5","explain":"When multiplying powers with the same base, add exponents: 2+3=5."},
      {"type":"mc","q":"Which pair gives the solutions of x² + 10x + 25 = 0?","choices":["x = 5 and x = 5","x = -4 and x = -5","x = -5 and x = -4","x = -5 and x = -5"],"answer":"x = -5 and x = -5","explain":"The quadratic factors as (x - (-5))(x - (-5)) = 0."},
      {"type":"mc","q":"Simplify 5^2 × 5^4.","choices":["5^8","5^1","5^6","10^6"],"answer":"5^6","explain":"When multiplying powers with the same base, add exponents: 2+4=6."},
      {"type":"mc","q":"Which pair gives the solutions of x² + 0x + -4 = 0?","choices":["x = -2 and x = 2","x = 3 and x = -2","x = 2 and x = -2","x = 2 and x = -1"],"answer":"x = 2 and x = -2","explain":"The quadratic factors as (x - (2))(x - (-2)) = 0."}
